## Downloads (decode/byte comparison on host)
PASS http        :: source.mp4 via HTTP engine, md5 c0d3be69b293fe8e2409a14b7e747161 == source
PASS hls-ts      :: EMU-HLS.ts 955040 B == concat of 10 segments (byte-identical)
PASS hls-dual    :: EMU-HLS.mp4 native remux on x86_64; video decode md5 == source, audio decode md5 == HLS audio rendition
PASS dash        :: EMU-DASH.mp4 video md5 9823e36fff60b0c882bf6f4df16cc2b8 == source; audio PCM prefix-equal to DASH reference, trim 1041 samples (same as device)
FAIL->PASS killresume (first run is a test-timing artifact, not a product failure):
   run 1 killed at 14 s: no segment had sealed yet (each ~16 s at 6 KB/s) -> restart refetched all 10 segments, no manifest; output byte-identical (O5b limit as registered)
   run 2 killed at 26 s: restart showed 50%; requests after restart seg001 seg003 seg005 seg007 seg009 only (no manifest); output byte-identical
PASS pause       :: paused row Stopped/Resume at 72%; requests while paused 23->23; resume fetched 6 unfinished media chunks only (no mpd, no init); video md5 == source
PASS pubdash     :: Akamai bbb_30fps 180p: 21210186 B, 634.566667 s, decode errors none; video md5 9818f1b98846fa24753dcb7074c68404 (== real-device result)
PASS pubhls      :: Mux x36xhzz 240p: 22418060 B, 634.633333 s, decode errors none; md5 d3888da6aa50f2ef29494310403e20d6 (== real-device result)

## UI (screenshots, light + dark)
Dark mode via a temporary test build forcing COLOR_MODE_DARK in EntryAbility (reverted; system settings untouched).
Found and fixed:
 - dark: category icons, file-type row icons and toolbar search/menu glyphs stayed black on dark background (the reported
   "background and text the same colour") -> SymbolGlyph fontColor text_primary
 - empty-list placeholders hard-coded in Chinese under the English UI -> string resources empty_finished/empty_in_progress
 - unknown ETA rendered "Time left: 00:00:00" -> "---"
 - non-modal Download Complete window had no close control and followed the user across pages -> Close button
Re-checked dark: main window, New Download, progress window, Download Complete, Settings (General/Network), Media grabber: readable.

